cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository redistributes published third-party atlases as demonstration
  material. If you use one of these datasets in your work, cite the study it
  came from: each Cellucid-ready AnnData store anndata/<id>.zarr names that
  study in uns['cellucid'] under `source` and `citation`, with its name, its URL
  and the citation to use. For Cellucid itself, the viewer that reads these
  datasets, cite the reference under preferred-citation.
type: dataset
title: "Cellucid demo datasets: public atlases as Cellucid-ready AnnData for the Cellucid viewer"
# No `version:` field, by design. This catalog carries no released versions: a
# store is republished whenever its pinned build or the writer that wrote it
# changes, and the build record that produced it is sources/<id>.json. The
# versioned companions are the Python (theislab/cellucid-python) and R
# (theislab/cellucid-r) packages, whose CITATION.cff files do carry `version:`.
#
# No `license:` field either, and for the reason `LICENSE` sets out at length:
# this repository has no single one. Its own material is BSD-3-Clause, and the
# datasets under anndata/ stay under the terms of the studies they were derived
# from. A single value here would have to misstate one of them.
authors:
  - family-names: Inecik
    given-names: Kemal
    email: k.inecik@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/theislab/cellucid-datasets"
url: "https://www.cellucid.com"
# BEGIN cellucid preferred-citation
# The single source of the Cellucid citation. It is written only in
# theislab/cellucid/CITATION.cff and copied verbatim into every other Cellucid
# repository's CITATION.cff; the README citations, the documentation's
# "Citing Cellucid" page, and the R package's inst/CITATION are generated from
# it. Never edit a copy.
#
# PLACEHOLDER while there is no `doi:`. Every generated citation says so for as
# long as `doi:` is absent. When the bioRxiv preprint is published:
#   1. set the real `title`, the full `authors` list, `doi`, and `year`, and
#      change `status` to `preprint`;
#   2. from the workspace, run
#        python cellucid-private/scripts/sync_citation.py
#      then `python cellucid-private/scripts/sync_citation.py --check`;
#   3. commit every repository it changed.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  status: in-preparation
  title: "PLACEHOLDER: Cellucid preprint, title to be announced (forthcoming on bioRxiv)"
  authors:
    - family-names: "Inecik"
      given-names: "Kemal"
  journal: "bioRxiv"
# END cellucid preferred-citation
